body:
Hi, heads up: this can return a `nullptr` if the window does not exist.

I'd do an early return for `p_ss->pointer_data.pointed_id == DisplayServer::INVALID_WINDOW_ID` and add an `ERR_FAIL_NULL` on the returned `*surface* variable:


```suggestion
	if(p_ss->pointer_data.pointed_id == DisplayServer::INVALID_ID) {
		return;
	}
	struct wl_surface *surface = window_get_wl_surface(p_ss->pointer_data.pointed_id);
	ERR_FAIL_NULL(surface);
```

I've not tested this, hopefully I didn't miss anything 😅

